{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T06:09:22.085Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cbb285dba71f705676688611","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.318","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1667"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1667: sdk/graph does not export ProjectedGraphResult, the public return type of runGraph, and the merge conflict_resolution union has no public name, so extensions derive both"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1667 (reported 2026-11-04 against 2026.11.4, TypeScript NodeNext, strict, skipLibCheck false). import type { ProjectedGraphResult } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/graph' and import type { MergeConflictResolution } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/merge' both fail with TS2305. Source confirms it: ProjectedGraphResult is exported from src/sdk/graph/run.ts and is the declared return type of runGraph, but src/sdk/graph/index.ts re-exports runGraph from run.js through a named list that omits the type, and sdk/public-surface.json records runGraph's signature as returning ProjectedGraphResult while the type itself is not on the surface. MergeDecisionReceipt in src/sdk/merge/receipts.ts types conflict_resolution inline with no public alias. Two fleet packages, pm-graph and pm-brief, independently derive the names with Awaited<ReturnType<typeof runGraph>> and an indexed access on MergeDecisionReceipt. Expected: ProjectedGraphResult is re-exported from sdk/graph and the aggregate entrypoint, the merge resolution union has a public name that the receipt declaration uses, and the SDK surface acceptance covers type-only imports next to the value-export parity checks. Why it matters for agents and extension authors: derived aliases break silently when the internal shape moves, and every extension author repeats the workaround. Related closed work covers values only: pm-obbh43 (GH-740) made the aggregate barrel complete for value exports of declared subpaths, and pm-suhxny derived the surface denominator from the export map, but neither checks that a type named in a public signature is itself importable. Duplicate check: searched SDK named type exports, ProjectedGraphResult, type-only surface acceptance, MergeDecisionReceipt and the aggregate entrypoint across all statuses, and no item owns missing public type names."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","extensions","gh:1667","sdk","types"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-05T06:09:22.085Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T06:09:22.085Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"import type { ProjectedGraphResult } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/graph' and from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk' compile under NodeNext with strict and skipLibCheck false; The conflict_resolution union of MergeDecisionReceipt has an exported public name (for example MergeConflictResolution) that the receipt declaration uses, importable from sdk/merge and from the aggregate entrypoint; The SDK surface gate fails when a type referenced by an exported function's public signature is not importable from the same entrypoint, with a negative control that removes one such re-export; A packed-consumer fixture with type-only imports of these names runs beside the existing value-export parity checks"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"In a NodeNext strict project with skipLibCheck false: import type { ProjectedGraphResult } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/graph' fails with TS2305"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Types named in public SDK signatures are importable by name from the entrypoint that exports the function"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"TS2305 for ProjectedGraphResult from sdk/graph and for a merge conflict-resolution alias from sdk/merge"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.11.4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-obbh43","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-05T06:09:22.085Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-suhxny","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-05T06:09:22.085Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8091f1414a06fe76fac928b6afda13c0b615274105b96396cb3b427860306e14","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Triage GitHub issue #1667 into the tracker","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b0079f16a5132b0d2cafc2d12bc3d3250c1d345a6f51ff8f4aa50e57bec1872b"}
